              "inline_data": null,
              "text": "In Massachusetts, the maximum amount you can collect for standard Unemployment Insurance (UI) depends on whether you have dependents and how long you are eligible to receive benefits. \n\n### 1. Maximum Weekly Benefit Amount\n* **Base Maximum:** The maximum weekly benefit is **$1,105 per week** (excluding dependency allowances). This rate went into effect on October 5, 2025, and remains active through October 2026, when Massachusetts typically adjusts its rates annually.\n* **Dependency Allowance:** If you are the main support for eligible dependents (e.g., children under 18, full-time students under 24, or disabled dependents), you can receive an additional **$25 per week per dependent**. This dependency allowance is capped at **50% of your weekly benefit amount**.\n\n### 2. Maximum Duration (Number of Weeks)\n* **Standard Duration:** Normally, you can collect benefits for up to **26 weeks**.\n* **Extended State Duration:** Under Massachusetts law, if the 12-month average unemployment rate in any of the state's major metropolitan areas rises above 5.1%, the maximum duration automatically increases to **30 weeks**. This extension was triggered in 2025, meaning eligible claimants can receive up to 30 weeks of benefits.\n\n### 3. Maximum Total Amount (The Cap)\nYour total maximum benefit credit for the benefit year is capped at either **30 times your weekly benefit amount** OR **36% of your total wages during your base period** (whichever is less). \n\nAt the absolute maximum weekly rate ($1,105) for the maximum period of 30 weeks:\n* **Without dependents:** You can collect up to **$33,150** in a benefit year ($1,105 x 30 weeks). *(If the state duration drops back to the standard 26 weeks, the max is $28,730)*.\n* **With dependents:** Because of the $25 per-dependent allowance, your total payout can be higher depending on how many dependents you claim. \n\n*(Note: If you are looking for **Paid Family and Medical Leave (PFML)** rather than standard unemployment, that is a separate state program. The maximum weekly benefit for PFML in Massachusetts is **$1,230.39**).*",
